# Line-ending policy.
#
# Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true) must not corrupt files that Linux
# executes: a CRLF working-tree copy of arachnea-docker/docker-entrypoint.sh
# was copied verbatim into the Docker image, its shebang became `#!/bin/sh\r`
# and tini died in a restart loop with
#   [FATAL tini (7)] exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh failed:
#   No such file or directory
# because the kernel searched for an interpreter literally named `/bin/sh\r`.
# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are therefore pinned to LF on every checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts stay CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
